separate their waste for recycling into  the different boxes and then the crew  come along and they have separated again  into the correct compartment on the  lorry here at the bulking station the  materials are unloaded into individual  Bay's before being prepared for  transportation to the recycling  factories let's take a look inside so  here we have our huge paper mountain  it's only taken three days for us to  collect this amount of paper each month  we can collect over 300 tons of  newspapers magazines paper that's from  householders and from recycling banks  when you consider it takes 15 trees to  make just one ton of paper  we're potentially saving over 4,500  trees every month this paper will be  collected and taken to Alfred and Kent  to a huge paper mill where it'll be  recycled into new newsprint did you know  it only takes seven days for a newspaper  to be recycled into a new one  all of the glass bottles and jars that  are collected in your green curbside  recycling boxes will be bought here to  the bulking station it will then be  transported to abel mouth where by using  special lasers they will be able to  separate the glass into the different  colors once separated it can then be  sent to various factories throughout the  UK to be made into new glass bottles and  jars did you know that if you recycle  just one of these glass jars you will  save enough energy to power a television  for one and a half hours  so here you can see all of the aluminium  cans and aerosols that we've collected  through the black curbside recycling box  once they're here at the Vulcan station  we have to separate the aluminium cans  from the steel cans and we do this using  a huge Council to machine with the  magnetic belt inside it can separate the  two materials and then it crushes them  and we can put them into bales which  makes it easy for transporting the  aluminium cans were taken to Warrington  where they'll be melted down amazing to  just simply new aluminium cans 